            "review_title": "Review at Nomu",
            "review_text": "Trevor K\n63 contributions\n0\nNot a genuine izakaya, but good\nJul 2022\nWhile I certainly had some toothsome dishes at Nomu, to call it an izakaya is misnomer. \n\nNomu is an upscale (rather pricey) Japanese-fusion, small plates restaurant. It also requires reservations and lacks the “hum” of a traditional izakaya. \n\nThe two cocktails I ordered were strong, and most of what I ate was delicious. I particularly enjoyed the blue crab fritters and seared, chilled beef. \n\nOne thing to remember if you dine here, come as a couple or with an even number of guests as most dishes are served with only two portions. \n\nMy party consisted of 3 people and it irked me that they couldn’t modify the portion sizes for one additional guest (even if a surcharge was included). \n\nLastly, the service was prompt and mostly attentive. \n\n*Note: this review is for Nomu’s D1 location. From what I can tell, the D1 and D2 locations are identical.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten July 15, 2022",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-10",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
